    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-070 — Font weight + font style pipeline.** The UA stylesheet already declared `h1-h6 { font-weight: bold }`, `em/i/cite/var { font-style: italic }`, `strong/b { font-weight: bold }`, and the cascade already stored these in `ComputedStyle`. But `LineFragment` / `StyledWord` / `LayoutText` had no fields to carry them, and Pango's `make_layout` only called `set_family` + `set_absolute_size`. **The comment in `ua_stylesheet.cpp` — *\"they do not flow into LayoutText yet\"* — was literally correct. ADR-070 answers that comment.**\n\n## Two commits on this branch\n\n1. **`4d0ce3d` — `chore(diagnostic)`:** `RenderPipeline::dump_layout_stats()` (HONEYBEE_DUMP_DOM env var) + this ADR as **Proposed**. The diagnostic is what surfaced the gap; retained as an ongoing tool.\n2. **`feat(render)` — this commit:** implementation + Implementation section appended.\n\n**Process note:** ADR-070 was initially drafted implementation-first at user prompt. User caught it and requested spec-first. Corrected to two-commit flow — spec lands with diagnostic, implementation lands after.\n\n## The pipeline (7 files, ~100 lines)\n\n**Data model** (`layout_box.hpp` + `text_utils.hpp`):\n- `LineFragment`, `LayoutText`, `StyledWord` gain `int font_weight = 400;` + `bool italic = false;`\n\n**Cascade propagation** (`layout.cpp`):\n- `parse_font_weight(std::string_view, int parent)` — `\"bold\"`→700, `\"normal\"`→400, `100..900`, `\"bolder\"`/`\"lighter\"` relative\n- Three insertion points: block capture, inline walker (`flatten_inline_to_words` signature extended), per-element override (same pattern as color), fragment emit\n\n**Pango** (`pango_text.cpp`):\n- `make_layout` gains defaulted `(int font_weight = 400, bool italic = false)`\n- Calls `pango_font_description_set_weight(static_cast<PangoWeight>(font_weight))` + `set_style`\n\n**Fragment merge** (`text_utils.cpp`):\n- `same_style` now checks weight + italic — adjacent words of different style don't merge\n\n## Verified (fixture screenshot 2026-11-04)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| h1 large + bold | ✅ (was flat before) |\n| h2 medium + bold | ✅ |\n| h3 small + bold | ✅ |\n| h4 body-size + bold | ✅ |\n| `<b>`, `<strong>` bold | ✅ |\n| `<em>`, `<i>` italic | ✅ |\n| `<cite>`, `<var>` italic | ✅ |\n| `<code>` monospace | ✅ |\n| Nested `<b><em>` = bold italic | ✅ |\n\nFirst time these render visually distinct from body text on HoneyBee.\n\n## Wikipedia status (honest)\n\nSuccessful run, smooth scroll, no crash, all previously-rendering content intact. **Explicit \"are headings now bold\" observation not captured this session** — the fixture is the primary proof that the pipeline works. If Wikipedia headings remain flat, that's a cascade-specificity issue (MediaWiki's author CSS overriding the UA sheet), not an ADR-070 defect. Next-session task to confirm.\n\n## What this ADR does NOT do\n\n- **`measure_with_pango` extension.** Bold text laid out at regular-weight metrics. Accept ~2–5% width drift on bold content until dedicated font-metrics ADR. Documented in spec.\n- **`vertical-align: super/sub`.** Reference markers still baseline-sized. ADR-071.\n- **`text-decoration`.** `<u>`, `<s>`, `<del>`, `<ins>` remain unstyled. ADR-072.\n- **Unit tests for cascade → Pango.** Verification is fixture + visual. No headless styling test infra yet.\n\n## Test count\n\n691 / 2641 unchanged (visual verification via fixture, not unit tests).\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Production-visual, fixture-verified** (8/8 checks pass), Wikipedia heading-bold confirmation deferred to next session with honest reporting.\n\nRefs #275\n",
